speechtext:
Whereas redistribution as outlined by the Prime Minister at the last session of parliament has not yet been carried into effect;
And whereas the principle of the transferable (or alternative) vote has been accepted by parliament, and the Prime Minister has promised to embody it in the Dominion Elections Act during the present session;
And whereas there have been several multimembered constituencies in the past and may also be after the

Proportional Representation
impending redistribution;
Therefore be it resolved, that, in the opinion of this House, the Dominion Elections Act be so amended as to use the transferable vote to secure, as far as possible, proportional representation in such multi-membered constituencies as may be provided for in the next redistribution.
